# omaishort

This is a Story → short-drama engine, not a TikTok clone.

- Do not emit one image per sentence. A scene has `duration_sec` plus 1–3 `shots` that share one `still_id`. Camera/motion (wide, zoom_in, pan) happens on that still.
- Characters exist only in the Character Bible. Scenes reference `character_ids`. Image prompts are composed from bible appearance/clothing plus scene fields.
- Drama beats are hook / conflict / rising_action / twist / ending. Never a fun-fact or explainer arc.
- Providers are protocols: LLM (OpenAI-compatible), image (ComfyUI → API → placeholder), TTS (ElevenLabs optional, edge-tts default). Do not hardcode a vendor in the planner.
- MVP render is FFmpeg Ken Burns 1080×1920. Remotion only consumes `timeline.json` (`elements`, `text`, `audio`).
- Job stages: analyze → plan → refs → stills → tts → captions → render.
- After TTS, rescale scene/shot times to the real audio duration.

Schema: `packages/schema/omaishort_schema/models.py`. Product: `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md`. Sources: `docs/RESEARCH.md`.
